id: records/2026-09-04-externalized-cognition-resurfacing-and-agency-loop
title: "Externalized cognition, relevance resurfacing, and the theory carrying its builder"
kind: clarification-record
status: proposed-canonical-backfill
recorded: 2026-09-04
supersedes_history: false
mutationAuthorized: false
externalEffectsAuthorized: false

source_observation: >
  A long multi-model design dialogue converged on a narrower product center:
  YAWN should help a person externalize cognition into a faithful, navigable,
  dynamic, AI-native symbol system that preserves relationships, provenance,
  uncertainty, time, and authority; frontier intelligence can then operate on
  that structure with the person rather than forcing the person to repeatedly
  reconstruct it from memory or prose.

product_center:
  statement: >
    Externalize cognition into a navigable living symbol system without
    pretending the symbol system is cognition or reality.
  experience:
    - "I can speak naturally."
    - "Something that mattered becomes visible outside me."
    - "I can inspect and correct it."
    - "It persists across time and intelligence providers."
    - "It reconnects to earlier models when they become relevant."
    - "Intelligence can deliberate and act on that structure with me."
    - "I do not need to hold the entire structure to remain its principal."

relationship_language:
  opening: "Here we are."
  holding: "What can I hold for you?"
  attention: "I think this matters now. Here's why. What do you see?"
  agency: "What do you want to do?"
  proof: "What happened?"
  boundary: >
    Shared orientation does not imply shared authority, values, identity, or
    ownership. The rightful principal remains explicit.

symbolization:
  rule: >
    Do not collapse all extracted structure into concepts. Ordinary expression
    may yield people, Agents, concepts, events, claims, questions, commitments,
    objectives, resources, constraints, evidence, lacunae, and relationships.
  concept: >
    A concept is a relatively stable reusable symbolic handle for a distinction
    worth naming. The same concept may participate in many Yawns without being
    duplicated.
  distinction: >
    A distinction is first an attributed differentiating operation or event;
    it does not automatically become a new canonical primitive, Yawn, or bot.
  relationship: >
    Relationships situate symbolic handles and may carry roles, commitments,
    expectations, authority, boundaries, dependencies, exchange, history,
    tension, trust, evidence, and current state.
  slash: >
    A / B means inspect the modeled relationship at that coordinate. It does not
    intrinsically mean containment, child, ownership, authority, or causation.

conversation_compilation:
  sequence:
    - natural_expression
    - attributed_observations
    - provisional_symbolic_handles
    - provisional_relationships
    - interpretations_and_lacunae
    - dialogue
    - ratification_correction_or_hold_open
    - model_update
    - optional_persistent_orientation_loop
  invariant: >
    Human expression remains natural; the ontology performs decomposition. The
    system should surface only the distinctions or relationships whose review
    materially changes orientation, authority, or action.

relevance_triggered_resurfacing:
  provisional_name: "relevance-triggered resurfacing"
  definition: >
    A present observation, question, concept, relationship, person, objective,
    decision, place, or event reactivates previously externalized cognition
    because that prior structure may materially improve current orientation.
  not_equal_to:
    - generic_search
    - reminder
    - context_window_recall
  preservation:
    - original_source
    - historical_epistemic_status
    - historical_relationships
    - what_changed_since
  historical_identity_rule: >
    Past Dave is not automatically present Dave. Resurfaced models may be
    reaffirmed, revised, rejected, superseded, or left context-specific.
  ranking_dimensions:
    - semantic_relevance
    - relationship_relevance
    - active_lacuna
    - current_objective
    - expected_information_gain
    - historical_importance
    - evidence_quality
    - freshness_or_decay
    - prior_user_acceptance
    - interruption_cost

stop_bleeding_intelligence:
  objective: >
    Preserve what was discovered, why it mattered, what it related to, where it
    came from, who believed it, what was inferred, what remained unresolved,
    what changed it, what happened afterward, and when it could matter again.
  failure_signal: >
    Repeated user prompts equivalent to "didn't we already establish this?" are
    evidence that the system is failing to carry durable cognition.

holarchy:
  preserve_current_contract: true
  recursion_rule: >
    A lacuna or subproblem earns its own Yawn only when resolving it requires an
    independently meaningful orientation loop with persistent state,
    relationships, movement or holding, and proof. A detected concept or
    question alone does not create a bot.
  bot_rule: >
    Additional Agents or Yawnbots are justified by parallel cognition, distinct
    capabilities, separate permission boundaries, independent responsibility,
    or persistent work—not by noun count.
  root_role: >
    The root detects, routes, relates, protects, and proposes. Local Yawns hold
    local frontiers; root orientation compares compressed attention claims
    rather than flattening everything into one global backlog.

attention_and_time:
  thesis: >
    A durable model that cannot know when to return something to attention is
    incomplete.
  attention_contract_fields:
    - holding_state
    - wake_conditions
    - event_dependencies
    - review_after
    - deadline
    - trajectory_if_ignored
    - urgency
    - interruption_cost
    - preferred_surface
    - escalation_policy
    - stop_conditions
  learning_signals:
    - "not now"
    - "you should have told me earlier"
    - "do not interrupt me for this"
    - "email me about things like this"
    - "this matters more than you think"

next_move_and_dialogue:
  goal: >
    Surface the smallest useful possibility set and identify the current
    highest-leverage next move while preserving human choice and inspectability.
  leverage_dimensions:
    - expected_progress
    - information_gain
    - downstream_unlocks
    - time_sensitivity
    - reversibility
    - cost
    - risk
    - friction
    - dependencies
    - confidence
  rule: >
    Leverage is an attributed hypothesis, not an oracle score. Material
    recommendations expose why, why now, evidence, assumptions, alternatives,
    uncertainty, and what would change the ranking.
  disagreement: >
    Human or Agent disagreement may reveal a missing concept, relationship,
    evidence item, objective, authority boundary, ranking weight, or lacuna.
    Preserve the discrepancy rather than smoothing it away.

recursive_improvement:
  seed: >
    Recommendation -> rationale -> dialogue -> discrepancy -> classified update
    -> move -> consequence -> proof -> prediction error -> better future model.
  widening_scope:
    - episode
    - local_yawn
    - person_model
    - relationship
    - reusable_yawn
    - canonical_ontology
  rule: >
    Evidence and rightful authority requirements increase as an update widens in
    scope. Local learning is cheap; canonical mutation is expensive.

simulation_and_calibration:
  role: >
    Simulation is a bounded verification tool for consequential choices, not the
    center of the system. Use premortems, counterfactuals, assumption
    perturbation, and adversarial review to challenge recommendations.
  boundaries:
    - "simulated consequence != observed consequence"
    - "model agreement != independent evidence"
    - "prediction != proof"
  calibration: >
    Record predicted outcomes and confidence before meaningful moves, then score
    them against observed consequence and proof so future confidence can become
    empirically calibrated.

health_pressure_test:
  purpose: >
    Health is a deliberately difficult arena for testing whether YAWN improves
    orientation without creating diagnosis theater, privacy leakage, overload,
    or silent authority transfer.
  test_goal: >
    Help a user externalize a confusing health situation into an inspectable
    model, preserve sensitive longitudinal information safely, understand major
    uncertainties and competing branches, choose high-information or
    professional-care moves, and reduce cognitive overwhelm.
  rules:
    - "probability is not diagnosis or truth"
    - "prefer information moves when they reduce uncertainty more safely than intervention"
    - "preserve source, supporting and contradictory evidence, uncertainty, and authority"
    - "use least-necessary disclosure and provider-independent durable state"
  success_experience: >
    The health arena may remain complex while the user no longer has to hold it
    as one undifferentiated problem; YAWN holds the branches and returns only
    what currently deserves attention.

value_hypothesis:
  claim: >
    A relationship-aware, provenance-preserving, holonic external symbol system
    with frontier intelligence, relevance-triggered resurfacing, explainable
    attention allocation, path dialogue, and proof-based calibration can
    increase effective agency while reducing cognitive carrying cost.
  status: predicted
  falsifiers:
    - "maintaining YAWN costs more cognition than it returns"
    - "resurfacing is frequently irrelevant or misses important prior cognition"
    - "dialogue corrections do not reduce repeated errors"
    - "ranked moves do not improve orientation or useful action"
    - "provenance and authority boundaries degrade through automation"

success_criteria:
  - "Natural speech can become useful symbolic structure without manual ontology entry."
  - "The user can navigate and cheaply correct that structure."
  - "Stable symbolic identity survives conversations, time, and provider changes."
  - "Important prior cognition resurfaces when relevant without manual search."
  - "The user can stop rehearsing important state merely to avoid losing it."
  - "Only a small explainable set of attention claims is surfaced at once."
  - "Recommendations support dialogue before adoption."
  - "Choice, holding, rejection, and delegation remain distinct."
  - "Consequences and proof update future confidence."
  - "The user spends progressively less time maintaining the system itself."
  - "The user can open the root Yawn, trust the current orientation, and make the next highest-leverage move."

primary_test:
  source: "the multi-model 2026-09-03/04 design conversation"
  instruction: >
    Ingest the conversation with exact attribution, reconcile extracted symbols
    and claims against canonical YAWN rather than duplicating them, preserve
    important distinctions and lacunae, and prove that the user can later
    recover the right piece of this shared work when it becomes relevant.
  success_question: >
    Can the user stop mentally maintaining the thread without losing the
    distinctions that matter?

